{"name":"Shrinking Violet","hex":"#5d84b1","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shrinking violet","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very shy or timid person, who avoids contact with others if possible. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shrinking_violet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shrinking Violet (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Shrinking Violet is the sixth studio album by hard rock band L.A. Guns, first released on June 1, 1999, through Perris Records, and is the only L.A. Guns album with singer Jizzy Pearl. The album was reissued, with bonus tracks and new artwork, on May 24, 2010, through Favored Nations. The album was produced by former Guns N' Roses guitarist Gilby Clarke who also provided additional guitars on the track \"Dreamtime\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4b/LAGunsShrinkingViolet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shrinking_Violet_(album)"},{"title":"Shrinking","blocks":[{"text":"Shrinking is an American comedy-drama television series created by Bill Lawrence, Jason Segel, and Brett Goldstein. The series stars Segel as a grieving therapist who decides to become drastically more involved in his patients' lives. Harrison Ford, Jessica Williams, Christa Miller, Michael Urie, Luke Tennie, Lukita Maxwell, and Ted McGinley also star."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shrinking"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/4b/LAGunsShrinkingViolet.jpg/250px-LAGunsShrinkingViolet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4b/LAGunsShrinkingViolet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/4b/LAGunsShrinkingViolet.jpg/250px-LAGunsShrinkingViolet.jpg?utm_sou